{"compatibility":"minor","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: minor.

Protected data: `y`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

Changes: replaced the manual marginalized mixture likelihood implemented with `target += log_sum_exp(...)` and `bernoulli_lpmf(...)` by the equivalent built-in sampling statement `y ~ bernoulli(dot_product(cluster_weight, cluster_prob))`. This preserves the density because a mixture of Bernoulli distributions with simplex weights has marginal success probability equal to the weighted average of the component probabilities. No data changes were required.
","model_safe_stan":"// ForestDB translation: Indian Buffet Process
// SafeStan-compatible rewrite
// The marginalized Bernoulli mixture is collapsed to a Bernoulli likelihood
// with success probability dot_product(cluster_weight, cluster_prob).
data {
  int<lower=1> K;
  int<lower=1> N;
  array[N] int<lower=0, upper=1> y;
}
parameters {
  simplex[K] cluster_weight;
  vector<lower=0, upper=1>[K] cluster_prob;
}
model {
  real mix_prob;

  cluster_weight ~ dirichlet(rep_vector(1.0 / K, K));
  cluster_prob ~ beta(1, 1);

  mix_prob = dot_product(cluster_weight, cluster_prob);
  y ~ bernoulli(mix_prob);
}
generated quantities {
  int<lower=1, upper=K> cluster = categorical_rng(cluster_weight);
}
","data_safe_json":"{"K":3,"N":3,"y":[0,1,1]}","protected_variables":["y"]}
